      .question-text {
        align-items: flex-start;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }

      .details p {
        padding: 0 18px 24px 66px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div class="eyebrow">Cat care guide</div>
      <h1 id="page-title">Frequently asked cat questions</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Quick, practical answers for new and curious cat people, from daily routines to behavior clues.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-card" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-1" id="question-1">
          <span class="question-text"><span class="number">01</span>How much should I feed my cat?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="details-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Most adult cats do best with measured meals based on their weight, age, activity level, and food type. Use the food label as a starting point, then adjust with your veterinarian if your cat gains or loses weight.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-2" id="question-2">
          <span class="question-text"><span class="number">02</span>Why does my cat knead blankets or people?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="details-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often knead when they feel relaxed, affectionate, or ready to settle in for a nap.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-3" id="question-3">
          <span class="question-text"><span class="number">03</span>How often should I clean the litter box?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="details-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Scoop at least once daily and fully refresh the box on a regular schedule based on the litter type. A clean box supports good habits and makes it easier to notice health changes early.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-4" id="question-4">
          <span class="question-text"><span class="number">04</span>Do indoor cats need playtime?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="details-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Yes. Short daily play sessions give indoor cats exercise, mental enrichment, and a healthy outlet for hunting instincts. Wand toys, puzzle feeders, and climbing spaces are great options.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-5" id="question-5">
          <span class="question-text"><span class="number">05</span>What does slow blinking mean?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="details-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>A slow blink is usually a friendly, relaxed signal. You can slowly blink back to tell your cat you are calm and comfortable too.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

    faqItems.forEach((item) => {
      const button = item.querySelector(".question");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
        item.classList.toggle("is-open", !isExpanded);
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
